1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,682
This Power B I sample shows I T spending five point eight five percent above plan.

2
00:00:06,682 --> 00:00:09,605
Infrastructure is the clearest area for investigation.

3
00:00:09,605 --> 00:00:18,792
This presentation follows the figures from the overall budget gap to regional costs, forecast accuracy, and the accounting checks needed before acting.

4
00:00:19,042 --> 00:00:24,465
The business challenge is to monitor I T costs and explain deviations early.

5
00:00:24,465 --> 00:00:26,968
Actual expenditure shows what was recorded.

6
00:00:26,968 --> 00:00:33,226
The plan is the original budget, while each latest estimate is a separate forecast snapshot.

7
00:00:33,226 --> 00:00:38,233
Comparing all three supports budgeting and accountability without adding the scenarios together.

8
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:45,190
The analysis uses Microsoft's public I T Spend Analysis sample, with data credited to obvi Ence.

9
00:00:45,190 --> 00:00:51,879
It covers twenty fourteen and contains one hundred sixty six thousand two hundred sixteen fact records.

10
00:00:51,879 --> 00:00:58,151
The video combines original Power B I report images with charts recalculated from the model.

11
00:00:58,417 --> 00:01:03,236
The Excel source and the P B I X fact totals match.

12
00:01:03,236 --> 00:01:09,661
Preparation checks found no null fact fields, no exact duplicate rows, and no unmatched dimension keys.

13
00:01:09,661 --> 00:01:12,874
Numeric keys and dates were standardized for analysis.

14
00:01:12,874 --> 00:01:18,497
Negative and zero values were retained because deleting them would change the reported costs.

15
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:22,984
The model connects one fact table to seven reporting dimensions.

16
00:01:22,984 --> 00:01:28,065
These active relationships are many to one and use single direction filtering.

17
00:01:28,065 --> 00:01:31,452
Scenario separates actuals from the plan and forecasts.

18
00:01:31,452 --> 00:01:38,649
I T Area and Business Area are different dimensions, even when both contain a label called Infrastructure.

19
00:01:38,917 --> 00:01:45,327
The source Amount measure calculates year to date cost and applies a factor of zero point three.

20
00:01:45,327 --> 00:01:50,605
This analysis preserves that factor so the results match the Power B I report.

21
00:01:50,605 --> 00:01:55,507
Comparing unscaled Excel sums with the report cards would create an avoidable mismatch.

22
00:01:55,750 --> 00:01:59,084
Plan variance is actual cost minus planned cost.

23
00:01:59,084 --> 00:02:02,419
A positive result therefore means cost above plan.

24
00:02:02,419 --> 00:02:07,837
Dividing by the plan gives the percentage variance when the baseline is meaningful.

25
00:02:07,837 --> 00:02:14,922
Missing plan records and negative planning adjustments need separate flags before their percentages are used for ranking.

26
00:02:15,167 --> 00:02:20,131
Full year actual cost is two hundred fifty seven point five three million dollars.

27
00:02:20,131 --> 00:02:24,385
The original plan is two hundred forty three point two nine million.

28
00:02:24,385 --> 00:02:31,831
The difference is fourteen point two four million, or five point eight five percent above plan, across the full model scope.

29
00:02:32,083 --> 00:02:37,745
The trend view compares cumulative actual spend with the plan and the third latest estimate.

30
00:02:37,745 --> 00:02:43,785
Each point includes earlier months, so these lines should not be read as individual monthly spending.

31
00:02:43,785 --> 00:02:49,447
By December, the gap to the original plan reaches fourteen point two four million dollars.

32
00:02:49,708 --> 00:02:56,851
Functional is the largest I T area by actual cost, at seventy nine point seven two million dollars.

33
00:02:56,851 --> 00:03:01,613
B U Support and Infrastructure follow at about seventy five million each.

34
00:03:01,613 --> 00:03:08,359
This distribution sets the scale, while the variance comparison shows which large areas are exceeding their budgets.

35
00:03:08,625 --> 00:03:13,316
Infrastructure I T area reports seventy four point nine eight million dollars

36
00:03:13,316 --> 00:03:18,007
of actual cost against a plan of fifty point six six million.

37
00:03:18,007 --> 00:03:23,870
That is twenty four point three two million above plan, or about forty eight percent.

38
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:28,170
The underlying adjustments and subareas deserve review before selecting a response.

39
00:03:28,417 --> 00:03:32,345
Infrastructure's variance is larger than the organization's net budget gap.

40
00:03:32,345 --> 00:03:38,631
The other I T areas are collectively about ten point zero eight million dollars below plan.

41
00:03:38,631 --> 00:03:43,345
These offsets reduce the total variance to fourteen point two four million.

42
00:03:43,345 --> 00:03:46,488
A single headline percentage would hide that difference.

43
00:03:46,750 --> 00:03:52,256
The United States accounts for about eighty four point four percent of actual expenditure.

44
00:03:52,256 --> 00:04:00,122
It is twelve point eight nine million dollars above plan, while Europe is about two point one three million above.

45
00:04:00,122 --> 00:04:06,415
Europe has a slightly higher percentage variance, but the United States has the larger financial impact.

46
00:04:06,667 --> 00:04:11,231
Canada and Latin America are each about thirteen percent below plan.

47
00:04:11,231 --> 00:04:14,965
Australia and New Zealand are about seven percent below.

48
00:04:14,965 --> 00:04:19,945
These results could reflect savings or work that moved to another period.

49
00:04:19,945 --> 00:04:25,339
Service output and project delivery records are needed before calling the difference underutilization.

50
00:04:25,583 --> 00:04:32,994
Labor is the largest actual cost group at one hundred thirty six point six four million dollars.

51
00:04:32,994 --> 00:04:38,225
It represents about fifty three point one percent of net actual cost.

52
00:04:38,225 --> 00:04:41,713
Depreciation and amortization follow, then hardware and software.

53
00:04:41,713 --> 00:04:47,380
Cost concentration identifies where contract and staffing reviews could have the greatest reach.

54
00:04:47,625 --> 00:04:55,502
Shared Services records about four hundred thirty seven thousand dollars against a plan of one point zero four eight million.

55
00:04:55,502 --> 00:04:59,046
That is fifty eight point three percent below plan.

56
00:04:59,046 --> 00:05:03,379
Labor is also below plan, by about two point three percent.

57
00:05:03,379 --> 00:05:08,892
Confirm service volumes and allocation rules before treating either result as a repeatable saving.

58
00:05:09,125 --> 00:05:14,024
The third latest estimate is two hundred sixty point zero nine million dollars.

59
00:05:14,024 --> 00:05:20,054
Actual cost finishes about two point five seven million lower, a difference of roughly one percent.

60
00:05:20,054 --> 00:05:26,837
The second estimate is closer to the final actual, so later forecasts should still be checked for error.

61
00:05:27,083 --> 00:05:34,516
Networking reports fifteen point one nine million dollars of actual cost against a plan of eight point six three million.

62
00:05:34,516 --> 00:05:40,091
The gap is about six point five five million, or seventy five point nine percent.

63
00:05:40,091 --> 00:05:47,152
Review approved scope changes and vendor contracts to explain the difference, rather than assuming a cause from the chart.

64
00:05:47,417 --> 00:05:53,409
The Administrative cost group has negative planning adjustments and no actual scenario records.

65
00:05:53,409 --> 00:05:57,096
Core Infrastructure also has a negative plan total.

66
00:05:57,096 --> 00:06:01,706
Africa and Asia have actual records without an original plan.

67
00:06:01,706 --> 00:06:08,159
These cases need reconciliation, and ordinary positive budget percentages would give a misleading ranking.

68
00:06:08,417 --> 00:06:14,236
The original Power B I report provides trend, cost element, and plan variance pages.

69
00:06:14,236 --> 00:06:23,380
In a live review, begin with the same year and cost scope, select a region, then an I T area and subarea.

70
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:27,952
The filters support exploration, while these presentation images show fixed selections.

71
00:06:28,208 --> 00:06:35,423
The plan variance page shows about forty four point four percent for the Infrastructure Business Area selection.

72
00:06:35,423 --> 00:06:40,092
The Infrastructure I T Area comparison was about forty eight percent.

73
00:06:40,092 --> 00:06:42,214
Those figures use different dimensions.

74
00:06:42,214 --> 00:06:47,731
Naming the dimension and checking selections prevents the two results from being confused.

75
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:55,357
A repeatable review moves from the overview to a region, then an I T area, subarea, and cost group.

76
00:06:55,357 --> 00:06:58,068
Use the month filter to test timing.

77
00:06:58,068 --> 00:07:06,199
Keep the measures reusable, sort months by their period number, and reconcile the headline cards after changes to the reporting scope.

78
00:07:06,458 --> 00:07:11,066
The budget owner should reconcile Infrastructure adjustments and investigate Networking.

79
00:07:11,066 --> 00:07:15,673
Regional owners should start with the United States, then Europe.

80
00:07:15,673 --> 00:07:20,280
Service owners should validate below plan spending against delivered work.

81
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:27,651
Finance should track forecast error and budget variance over time, with named owners for each explanation.

82
00:07:27,917 --> 00:07:37,109
The organization is five point eight five percent above its annual plan, while actual cost is close to the third latest estimate.

83
00:07:37,109 --> 00:07:41,287
The strongest review combines financial impact with detailed scope checks.

84
00:07:41,287 --> 00:07:48,390
Follow the major drivers, validate exceptions, and use the same measures to judge the next reporting cycle.

